Chapter: StarMapWasm
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter CCE
  cites Starmap chapter CelestialTypes
  cites Starmap chapter StarCatalog
  cites Starmap chapter StarMapScene

 Browser entry point for the star map. The catalog is built once, into linear
 memory, by the entry act; every later call reads it back from there, so no
 frame allocates.

 We say:

Section: Memory Map

 The base addresses have to clear the data segment, which is where heap_start
 lands: the two modules we ship measured 71,635 and 71,531 bytes there, so 1 MB
 is a twelvefold margin that a larger string table cannot reach. sm-heap-floor
 is where the heap is advanced before anything allocates, because the heap
 otherwise grows straight through these buffers.

  sm-star-count : Integer = 256

  sm-label-count : Integer = 260

  sm-visible-count : Integer = 264

  sm-ready : Integer = 268

  sm-cam-state : Integer = 352

  sm-star-tab : Integer = 1048576

  sm-label-blob : Integer = 1114112

  sm-visible-buf : Integer = 1179648

  sm-heap-floor : Integer = 1245184

  sm-star-stride : Integer = 48

  sm-label-stride : Integer = 80

  sm-label-cap : Integer = 76

  sm-max-labels : Integer = 200

 65535 is the absent marker for a label slot and for a selection. It is above
 every object id and every label slot, which is what a sentinel read back
 through peek-32 has to be: the read zero-extends, so a negative marker is
 unreachable.

  sm-absent : Integer = 65535

Section: Word Access

 peek-32 zero-extends, so a value stored negative reads back as its unsigned
 image and sm-signed is the correction. A page reading the same words needs no
 correction, because an Int32Array is signed already.

 Coordinates reach 320,000,000,000 (parsecs x 1000, the far galaxies) and do
 not fit one word at all. sm-put-wide splits on 1,000,000: Integer division
 truncates toward zero, so quotient and remainder carry the same sign and
 recombine exactly, and both halves stay inside a word for every value the
 catalog holds.

  sm-signed : Integer -> Integer
  sm-signed (u) = if u >= 2147483648 then u - 4294967296 else u

  sm-put : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-put (base) (off) (v) = poke-32 base off v

  sm-get : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-get (base) (off) = sm-signed (peek-32 base off)

  sm-wide-split : Integer = 1000000

  sm-put-wide : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-put-wide (base) (off) (v) =
    let hi = v / sm-wide-split
    in let lo = v - hi * sm-wide-split
    in let w = sm-put base off lo
    in sm-put base (off + 4) hi

  sm-get-wide : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-get-wide (base) (off) = sm-get base off + sm-get base (off + 4) * sm-wide-split

Section: Star Record

 Offsets within one star record. x, y and z are wide and take two words each.

  sm-off-x : Integer = 0

  sm-off-y : Integer = 8

  sm-off-z : Integer = 16

  sm-off-mag : Integer = 24

  sm-off-rgb : Integer = 28

  sm-off-id : Integer = 32

  sm-off-size : Integer = 36

  sm-off-label : Integer = 40

  sm-off-kind : Integer = 44

  sm-kind-code : CelestialKind -> Integer
  sm-kind-code (k) = when k
    is CkStar -> 0
    is CkBinaryStar -> 1
    is CkGlobularCluster -> 2
    is CkOpenCluster -> 3
    is CkPlanetaryNebula -> 4
    is CkDiffuseNebula -> 5
    is CkGalaxy -> 6
    is CkQuasar -> 7
    is CkPulsar -> 8
    is CkBlackHole -> 9
    is CkPlanet -> 10
    is CkMoon -> 11
    is CkAsteroid -> 12
    is CkComet -> 13

Section: Label Blob

 A name is packed four bytes to a word because there is no poke-8. The bytes
 are Unicode: char-code-at answers a CCE code point, which is not what a page
 decoding UTF-8 means, so to-unicode converts at this boundary.

  sm-name-byte : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-name-byte (name) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0 else to-unicode (char-code-at name i)

  sm-write-name : Integer, Integer, Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-write-name (addr) (off) (name) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let b0 = sm-name-byte name i n
    in let b1 = sm-name-byte name (i + 1) n
    in let b2 = sm-name-byte name (i + 2) n
    in let b3 = sm-name-byte name (i + 3) n
    in let w = sm-put addr off (b0 + b1 * 256 + b2 * 65536 + b3 * 16777216)
    in sm-write-name addr (off + 4) name (i + 4) n

  sm-write-label : Integer, Text -> Integer
  sm-write-label (slot) (name) =
    let n = text-length name
    in if n == 0 then sm-absent
    else let cap = if n > sm-label-cap then sm-label-cap else n
    in let addr = sm-label-blob + slot * sm-label-stride
    in let w = sm-put addr 0 cap
    in let body = sm-write-name addr 4 name 0 cap
    in slot

Section: Building the Table

 The catalog is the fifty named stars with the Messier objects and the notable
 galaxies appended. catalog-all is the stars alone, which is why it is not what
 is read here.

  sm-catalog : List CelestialObj
  sm-catalog = scene-append-list (scene-append-list catalog-stars catalog-messier 0 (list-length catalog-messier)) catalog-galaxies 0 (list-length catalog-galaxies)

  sm-write-stars : List CelestialObj, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-write-stars (cat) (i) (n) (labels) =
    if i >= n then labels
    else let obj = list-at cat i
    in let addr = sm-star-tab + i * sm-star-stride
    in let w0 = sm-put-wide addr sm-off-x (obj.co-x)
    in let w1 = sm-put-wide addr sm-off-y (obj.co-y)
    in let w2 = sm-put-wide addr sm-off-z (obj.co-z)
    in let w3 = sm-put addr sm-off-mag (obj.co-mag)
    in let w4 = sm-put addr sm-off-rgb (bv-to-rgb (obj.co-bv))
    in let w5 = sm-put addr sm-off-id (obj.co-id)
    in let w6 = sm-put addr sm-off-size (co-screen-size obj 0)
    in let w7 = sm-put addr sm-off-kind (sm-kind-code (obj.co-kind))
    in let slot = if labels >= sm-max-labels then sm-absent else sm-write-label labels (obj.co-name)
    in let w8 = sm-put addr sm-off-label slot
    in let taken = if slot == sm-absent then labels else labels + 1
    in sm-write-stars cat (i + 1) n taken

Section: Camera State

 Offsets within the camera block. Focus and distance are wide.

  sm-cam-focus-x : Integer = 0

  sm-cam-focus-y : Integer = 8

  sm-cam-focus-z : Integer = 16

  sm-cam-yaw : Integer = 24

  sm-cam-pitch : Integer = 28

  sm-cam-dist : Integer = 32

  sm-cam-selected : Integer = 40

  sm-cam-objects : Integer = 44

  sm-cam-mag-limit : Integer = 48

  sm-cam-speed : Integer = 52

  sm-cam-fov : Integer = 56

  sm-cam-flags : Integer = 60

  sm-write-cam : StarCamera -> Integer
  sm-write-cam (cam) =
    let b = sm-cam-state
    in let a0 = sm-put-wide b sm-cam-focus-x (cam.sc-focus-x)
    in let a1 = sm-put-wide b sm-cam-focus-y (cam.sc-focus-y)
    in let a2 = sm-put-wide b sm-cam-focus-z (cam.sc-focus-z)
    in let a3 = sm-put b sm-cam-yaw (cam.sc-yaw)
    in let a4 = sm-put b sm-cam-pitch (cam.sc-pitch)
    in let a5 = sm-put-wide b sm-cam-dist (cam.sc-dist)
    in let a6 = sm-put b sm-cam-speed (cam.sc-speed)
    in sm-put b sm-cam-fov (cam.sc-fov)

  sm-read-cam : Integer -> StarCamera
  sm-read-cam (x) = StarCamera {
    sc-focus-x = sm-get-wide sm-cam-state sm-cam-focus-x,
    sc-focus-y = sm-get-wide sm-cam-state sm-cam-focus-y,
    sc-focus-z = sm-get-wide sm-cam-state sm-cam-focus-z,
    sc-yaw = sm-get sm-cam-state sm-cam-yaw,
    sc-pitch = sm-get sm-cam-state sm-cam-pitch,
    sc-dist = sm-get-wide sm-cam-state sm-cam-dist,
    sc-fov = sm-get sm-cam-state sm-cam-fov,
    sc-near = 1,
    sc-far = 100000000000,
    sc-speed = sm-get sm-cam-state sm-cam-speed,
    sc-target-name = ""
  }

Section: Keeping the Page's Entries Alive

 Only what the entry act transitively reaches is emitted, so a function the
 page calls and Codex does not would be dropped and its export would name
 nothing. Touching all sixteen here is what keeps them in the module, which is
 also what apps/fishtank/FishTankWasm.codex does under this name. It runs
 before the table is built and before the camera is written, so every cell it
 disturbs is overwritten by the rest of sm-init; do not move it later, and do
 not delete it for looking pointless.

  sm-keep-alive : Integer -> Integer
  sm-keep-alive (x) =
    sm-tick x + sm-orbit x x + sm-zoom x + sm-move-forward x + sm-move-right x + sm-move-up x + sm-set-speed x + sm-select-obj x + sm-fly-to x + sm-set-mag-limit x + sm-toggle-labels + sm-toggle-grid + sm-toggle-constellations + sm-get-star-count + sm-get-visible-count + sm-get-label-count

Section: Init

  sm-init : [Console] Integer
  sm-init = act
    adv <- __heap-advance sm-heap-floor
    let churn = sm-keep-alive 0
    in let mark = __heap-save
    in let cat = sm-catalog
    in let n = list-length cat
    in let labels = sm-write-stars cat 0 n 0
    in let back = __heap-restore mark
    in let c0 = sm-put 0 sm-star-count n
    in let c1 = sm-put 0 sm-label-count labels
    in let c2 = sm-write-cam camera-new
    in let c3 = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-selected) sm-absent
    in let c4 = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-objects) n
    in let c5 = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-mag-limit) 6000
    in let c6 = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-flags) 7
    in let vis = sm-tick 0
    in let rdy = sm-put 0 sm-ready 1
    in n
  end

Section: Tick

 The star table does not move, so a frame only re-selects which rows are
 visible under the magnitude limit and writes their indices. A page reads the
 rows it names straight out of the table.

  sm-tick : Integer -> Integer
  sm-tick (frame) =
    let n = sm-get 0 sm-star-count
    in let lim = sm-get 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-mag-limit)
    in let vis = sm-fill-visible 0 n lim 0
    in let w = sm-put 0 sm-visible-count vis
    in vis

  sm-fill-visible : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-fill-visible (i) (n) (lim) (out) =
    if i >= n then out
    else if out >= sm-max-labels then out
    else let src = sm-star-tab + i * sm-star-stride
    in if sm-get src sm-off-mag > lim then sm-fill-visible (i + 1) n lim out
    else let w = sm-put sm-visible-buf (out * 4) i
    in sm-fill-visible (i + 1) n lim (out + 1)

Section: Camera Controls

  sm-orbit : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-orbit (dyaw) (dpitch) = sm-write-cam (camera-orbit (sm-read-cam 0) dyaw dpitch)

  sm-zoom : Integer -> Integer
  sm-zoom (delta) = sm-write-cam (camera-zoom (sm-read-cam 0) delta)

  sm-move-forward : Integer -> Integer
  sm-move-forward (amount) = sm-write-cam (camera-move-forward (sm-read-cam 0) amount)

  sm-move-right : Integer -> Integer
  sm-move-right (amount) = sm-write-cam (camera-move-right (sm-read-cam 0) amount)

  sm-move-up : Integer -> Integer
  sm-move-up (amount) = sm-write-cam (camera-move-up (sm-read-cam 0) amount)

  sm-set-speed : Integer -> Integer
  sm-set-speed (s) = sm-write-cam (camera-set-speed (sm-read-cam 0) s)

Section: Selection

  sm-find-by-id : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sm-find-by-id (id) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then sm-absent
    else if sm-get (sm-star-tab + i * sm-star-stride) sm-off-id == id then i
    else sm-find-by-id id (i + 1) n

  sm-select-obj : Integer -> Integer
  sm-select-obj (id) =
    let n = sm-get 0 sm-star-count
    in let idx = sm-find-by-id id 0 n
    in if idx == sm-absent then sm-absent
    else let w = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-selected) id
    in idx

  sm-fly-to : Integer -> Integer
  sm-fly-to (id) =
    let n = sm-get 0 sm-star-count
    in let idx = sm-find-by-id id 0 n
    in if idx == sm-absent then sm-absent
    else let src = sm-star-tab + idx * sm-star-stride
    in let cam = sm-read-cam 0
    in let moved = camera-goto cam (sm-get-wide src sm-off-x) (sm-get-wide src sm-off-y) (sm-get-wide src sm-off-z) ""
    in let w = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-selected) id
    in let f = sm-write-cam moved
    in idx

Section: Toggles

 Bit 1 is labels, bit 2 the grid, bit 4 the constellation figures. They live in
 one word so a page reads the three with one load.

  sm-flag-labels : Integer = 1

  sm-flag-grid : Integer = 2

  sm-flag-constellations : Integer = 4

  sm-toggle-flag : Integer -> Integer
  sm-toggle-flag (bit) =
    let f = sm-get 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-flags)
    in let nf = if bit-and f bit == bit then f - bit else f + bit
    in let w = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-flags) nf
    in nf

  sm-toggle-labels : Integer
  sm-toggle-labels = sm-toggle-flag sm-flag-labels

  sm-toggle-grid : Integer
  sm-toggle-grid = sm-toggle-flag sm-flag-grid

  sm-toggle-constellations : Integer
  sm-toggle-constellations = sm-toggle-flag sm-flag-constellations

  sm-set-mag-limit : Integer -> Integer
  sm-set-mag-limit (mag) =
    let w = sm-put 0 (sm-cam-state + sm-cam-mag-limit) mag
    in sm-tick 0

Section: Queries

  sm-get-star-count : Integer
  sm-get-star-count = sm-get 0 sm-star-count

  sm-get-visible-count : Integer
  sm-get-visible-count = sm-get 0 sm-visible-count

  sm-get-label-count : Integer
  sm-get-label-count = sm-get 0 sm-label-count

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    n <- sm-init
    print-line-uni ("StarMap WASM: " & show n & " objects, " & show (sm-get 0 sm-label-count) & " labels, " & show (sm-get 0 sm-visible-count) & " visible")
  end

